  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Thundercat Technology has $154M in contract obligations for FY2027 to date. Thundercat Technology won 39 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $3.9M. Obligations fell 86.8% year over year. Historical obligations show larger prior-year totals: FY22 $680M, FY23 $854M, FY24 $804M, FY25 $913M, and FY26 $1.2B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer in FY2027 to date with $142M in obligations. Other buying agencies recorded much smaller totals, including the Department of Agriculture with $4.9M and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $3.9M. Market detail for FY2027 to date is concentrated in Other Computer Related Services at $154M, while Software Publishers shows $0. The dataset notes that current-year totals are partial and that most figures are contract obligations except where award-value totals are specifically called out. This snapshot highlights a sharp year-over-year drop in obligations alongside continued concentration in a single industry and a single buying agency.",
